From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:26:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/37] Finder file chooser: Escape cancels from anywhere;
 installer fixes the portal setting

Escape is caught for the whole picker before the file view or a text field
can take it (an open dropdown still closes first). finder-extras/install.sh
now sets org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser=finder;kde in
kde-portals.conf whether the file is missing, has another FileChooser
choice, or has none, keeping the user's other portal choices.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KdkdNUmoM62iDwjRop6X5f
---
 README.md                                   |  5 +++++
 finder-extras/install.sh                    | 14 ++++++++----
 src/finder/filechooser/finderfiledialog.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++----
 src/finder/filechooser/finderfiledialog.h   |  1 +
 4 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f7fe6ac82..793020dc9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -28,6 +28,11 @@ Based on Dolphin 26.08.1. Every Finder change is a commit on top of the
   context menu, and a title and footer that follow the active column.
 - **Footer**: "16 items, 727 GB available" / "1 of 16 selected", with the
   zoom slider.
+- **Open/Save windows for other apps**: browsers, Flatpak and Snap apps
+  and others that ask the desktop for a file dialog get a Finder-style one
+  (sidebar, list/icon views, Save As, file types; Escape cancels). The
+  installer registers it with xdg-desktop-portal (KDE's dialog stays as the
+  fallback; KDE apps keep their own dialog).
 - **AirDrop** with iPhones and Macs: AirDrop in the sidebar (Ctrl+Shift+R),
   right-click › Share › AirDrop, progress cards for sending and receiving,
   and notifications. See below.
diff --git a/finder-extras/install.sh b/finder-extras/install.sh
index 2f26cb6d5..ddec510d6 100755
--- a/finder-extras/install.sh
+++ b/finder-extras/install.sh
@@ -39,11 +39,17 @@ services=${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/dbus-1/services
 mkdir -p "$services" "$config/xdg-desktop-portal"
 sed "s|@PREFIX@|$prefix|" "$root/finder-extras/org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.finder.service" \
     > "$services/org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.finder.service"
-if [ -f "$config/xdg-desktop-portal/kde-portals.conf" ]; then
-    grep -q 'FileChooser=finder' "$config/xdg-desktop-portal/kde-portals.conf" \
-        || echo "Add org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser=finder;kde under [preferred] in $config/xdg-desktop-portal/kde-portals.conf"
+# Point the portal's file chooser at Finder (KDE's dialog stays as fallback),
+# keeping any other portal choices already made in the user's file.
+conf=$config/xdg-desktop-portal/kde-portals.conf
+if [ ! -f "$conf" ]; then
+    cp "$root/finder-extras/kde-portals.conf" "$conf"
+elif grep -q '^org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser=' "$conf"; then
+    sed -i 's|^org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser=.*|org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser=finder;kde|' "$conf"
+elif grep -q '^\[preferred\]' "$conf"; then
+    sed -i '/^\[preferred\]/a org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser=finder;kde' "$conf"
 else
-    cp "$root/finder-extras/kde-portals.conf" "$config/xdg-desktop-portal/kde-portals.conf"
+    printf '\n[preferred]\ndefault=kde\norg.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser=finder;kde\n' >> "$conf"
 fi
 # xdg-desktop-portal only reads backend descriptions from its system folder.
 portal=/usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal/portals/finder.portal
